WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.238
The method borrows Boltzmann's idea of building the
distribution that maximizes entropy subject to fixed moments.

00:00:04.318 --> 00:00:08.556
Concretely,

00:00:08.636 --> 00:00:12.874
the generator is written as the exponential of a
polynomial in the observable,

00:00:12.954 --> 00:00:17.192
so its coefficients, the lambdas, are the moments
being unfolded.

00:00:17.272 --> 00:00:21.510
This generator reweights the simulated events,

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:25.828
and a discriminator neural network tries to tell
the reweighted simulation apart from the real data.

00:00:25.908 --> 00:00:30.146
The two are trained against each other on a
weighted binary cross-entropy loss: the discriminator

00:00:30.226 --> 00:00:34.464
minimizes it while the generator maximizes it.

00:00:34.544 --> 00:00:38.782
Because the reweighting only changes importance
weights and not the event features,

00:00:38.862 --> 00:00:43.100
the expensive detector emulation runs a single time.
